@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Role-Based Access Control (RBAC)";
    ViewData["ActiveMenu"] = "AzureDevOps";
}

<div class="container py-4">
    <p class="text-center lead">Role-Based Access Control (RBAC) is a security model that restricts access to resources based on user roles, ensuring secure and controlled access management in Azure DevOps.</p>
    <hr />

    <div class="mt-5">
        <h2>Why Use RBAC in DevOps?</h2>
        <p>RBAC is essential for implementing a least privilege model, reducing security risks, and ensuring compliance with security policies. Key benefits include:</p>
        <ul>
            <li><strong>Improved Security:</strong> Prevents unauthorized access to critical resources.</li>
            <li><strong>Granular Permissions:</strong> Assigns precise access levels based on job roles.</li>
            <li><strong>Compliance & Auditing:</strong> Tracks and controls access for regulatory requirements.</li>
            <li><strong>Minimized Risk:</strong> Reduces exposure to potential security threats.</li>
            <li><strong>Operational Efficiency:</strong> Streamlines user access management and enhances collaboration.</li>
            <li><strong>Seamless Integration:</strong> Works with Active Directory and other identity management solutions.</li>
        </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="text-center mt-4">
        <img src="https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/role-based-access-control/media/rbac-overview.png" alt="RBAC Model" class="img-fluid rounded shadow-lg">
        <p class="text-muted mt-2"><small>RBAC in Azure DevOps</small></p>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-5">
        <h2>RBAC Roles in Azure DevOps</h2>
        <p>Azure DevOps provides predefined roles to manage access:</p>
        <ul>
            <li><strong>Project Administrators:</strong> Full control over project settings and security.</li>
            <li><strong>Contributors:</strong> Can modify and contribute to repositories and pipelines.</li>
            <li><strong>Readers:</strong> Read-only access to project resources.</li>
            <li><strong>Build Administrators:</strong> Manage build and release pipelines.</li>
            <li><strong>Stakeholders:</strong> Limited access for tracking work items.</li>
            <li><strong>Custom Roles:</strong> Organizations can define custom roles to fit unique security needs.</li>
        </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-5">
        <h3>Setting Up RBAC in Azure DevOps</h3>
        <p>Follow these steps to configure RBAC:</p>
        <ol>
            <li><strong>Go to Azure DevOps Portal:</strong> Navigate to the project settings.</li>
            <li><strong>Open Security Settings:</strong> Select the security tab to manage access.</li>
            <li><strong>Assign Roles:</strong> Choose a user and assign the appropriate role.</li>
            <li><strong>Review Access Policies:</strong> Ensure permissions align with security requirements.</li>
            <li><strong>Implement Group-Based Access:</strong> Assign roles to groups instead of individuals for better scalability.</li>
            <li><strong>Enable Audit Logging:</strong> Track role assignments and changes to ensure accountability.</li>
        </ol>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-5">
        <h3>Example YAML for RBAC Implementation</h3>
        <pre class="bg-light p-3 rounded">
steps:
- task: AzureRBAC@1
  inputs:
    azureSubscription: 'MyAzureSubscription'
    roleDefinitionName: 'Contributor'
    principalId: 'UserObjectID'
    scope: '/subscriptions/{subscriptionId}/resourceGroups/{resourceGroup}'
        </pre>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-5">
        <h3>Best Practices for RBAC</h3>
        <ul>
            <li><strong>Follow Least Privilege Principle:</strong> Assign only necessary permissions.</li>
            <li><strong>Review Access Regularly:</strong> Periodically audit user permissions.</li>
            <li><strong>Use Group-Based Access:</strong> Manage access through security groups.</li>
            <li><strong>Monitor Activity Logs:</strong> Track access changes for compliance.</li>
            <li><strong>Automate Role Assignments:</strong> Use scripts to manage RBAC policies efficiently.</li>
            <li><strong>Integrate with Identity Providers:</strong> Connect RBAC with Azure AD for centralized access control.</li>
            <li><strong>Implement Just-In-Time (JIT) Access:</strong> Grant temporary elevated access for sensitive tasks.</li>
            <li><strong>Use Conditional Access Policies:</strong> Restrict access based on user location, device, or security posture.</li>
        </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-5">
        <p>RBAC ensures secure and organized access control in Azure DevOps, allowing teams to maintain security and compliance while enabling collaboration. By following best practices, organizations can minimize risks and improve operational efficiency.</p>
    </div>

